0	section	Talking to Ali the Mayor
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Welcome, adventurer, to the town of Pollnivneach, the gateway to Menaphos and Al Kharid. My name is Ali and I'm the mayor of this town. I hope you enjoy your stay here.
1	line	Player	Thank you. That is one of the warmest welcomes I've ever had! People generally treat travelling adventurers with suspicion.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	All are welcome here. Now more than ever I suppose.
1	line	Player	What do you mean by that?
1	line	Ali the Mayor	There's trouble in town, and a lot of villagers have left as a result. Things are looking dire.
1	line	Player	I'm looking for someone called Ali.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Well, take your pick!
1	line	Player	I mean I'm looking for a specific Ali. He's Ali Morrisane's nephew.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Oh, that Ali! Well, er, your best bet is to ask around town. I'm sure someone will know what he's up to.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ali the Camel Man
1	line	Ali the Camel Man	Welcome to my discount camel store. Can I help you with anything?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	A discount camel store?
2	line	Player	A discount camel store?
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Yes - it's my great idea - selling camels at discounted prices so that the common man can experience the joys of owning a camel of their very own! They're not just a source of kebab meat you know!
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	So can I buy a camel then? I'm hungry!
3	line	Player	So can I buy a camel then? I'm hungry!
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	I would never sell one to the likes of you! They are beautiful, majestic creatures, not food! Get out of my shop.
3	action	end
2	option	Yes, camels are beautiful creatures.
3	line	Player	Yes, camels are beautiful creatures.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Ah, wondrous camels! Best of all Saradomin's creations. Ships of the desert, far more useful than any horse or donkey. Truly, they are a man's best friend.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Perhaps you'd like a camel of your own? You're in the right place, if so...
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Well yes, actually I would like to ask about something else.
4	action	initial
3	option	No, but thanks for your time.
4	line	Player	No, but thanks for your time.
4	action	end
2	option	Why would I want a camel? All they do is spit and...
3	line	Player	Why would I want a camel? All they do is spit and...
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Pah! I've seen mummies with more brains than you! If you treat camels badly then of course they're going to spit at you. May your robes never be clean again!
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
3	action	initial
2	option	Actually, I think I was a camel in a previous life.
3	line	Player	Actually, I think I was a camel in a previous life.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	You're teasing me now! You rogue!
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Everyone laughs at the poor Discount Camel Seller.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
3	action	initial
2	option	So is the discount camel business good then?
3	line	Player	So is the discount camel business good then?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Business is booming! Pollnivneach has never seen this number of visitors.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	In fact I'm thinking of expanding and trying to break into the camel hire market.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	If only I could figure out how to get people to return the camels...
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
3	action	initial
1	option	Tell me about this town.
2	line	Player	Tell me about this town.
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Well, Pollnivneach is a funny little place. It's a small town and you'd think it'd be nice and quiet.
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	But those Menaphites and bandits are making the place quite unbearable.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	In what way?
3	line	Player	In what way?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Well, one group is as bad as the other! They steal, they fight, they cause trouble with us locals. Just yesterday one of those bandits came looking for protection money!
3	line	Player	Why don't the authorities stop this?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	We're a small town. We don't have the resources to keep the gangs off our backs! Menaphos and Al Kharid are no help either.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	To tell the truth we live in hope that an outsider, someone with no ties to either group, could broker a deal to halt the hostilities between them.
3	line	Player	Hmm...
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
3	action	initial
2	option	Well the weak will always be trodden on. Why not stand up to them?
3	line	Player	Well the weak will always be trodden on. Why not stand up to them?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	That's a little unfair, my friend. We can't all be brave adventurers. If we were, where would you purchase quality camels at discounted prices?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	You might think about that. Anyway, isn't it the job of the brave adventurer to protect the weak and innocent from evil and harm?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
3	action	initial
2	option	Perhaps I could help.
3	line	Player	Perhaps I could help.
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Yes, perhaps you could.
3	line	Player	You know the politics better than I do. What do you recommend?
3	line	Ali the Camel Man	Me?! I am but a humble discount camel seller. You're the adventurer, don't you know what to do?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Of course I know what to do! I was just testing you!
4	line	Player	Of course I know what to do! I was just testing you!
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	That is reassuring to hear. Too often one meets brainless adventurers whose solution to every problem is to hack, maim and murder.
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	I'm glad to know you're not of that ilk.
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
4	action	initial
3	option	Perhaps I should know, but offered advice should never be shunned.
4	line	Player	Perhaps I should know, but offered advice should never be shunned.
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	The state of adventurers today. They need everything spelled out for them.
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	What, you want me to put a little note in your quest journal?
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	But fine, I'll give you a hint. Try and see if you can get the gangs to agree to a truce by offering them each a token gift as an act of reconciliation.
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	If that fails to work, you must consider trying to influence the gangs from within.
4	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
4	action	initial
1	option	Lovely day isn't it?
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	It's a beautiful day today, but word has it that it will rain tomorrow.
2	line	Player	Really?
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	No! When have you ever known it to rain here in Gielinor?
2	line	Player	Oh. Anyway...
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
2	action	above
1	option	Are those camels around the side for sale?
2	line	Player	Are those camels around the side for sale?
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Those two camels around the side are already sold.
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	I've got new stock coming very soon though. Come back later if you're still interested.
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Is there anything else I can help you with?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Well yes, actually I would like to ask about something else.
3	action	initial
2	option	No, but thanks for your time.
3	line	Player	No, but thanks for your time.
3	action	end
1	option	I'm looking for Ali from Pollnivneach.
2	line	Player	I'm looking for Ali from Pollnivneach.
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Well, you've found your man.
2	line	Player	Really? Do you have an uncle called Ali?
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Why yes - all my uncles are called Ali!
2	line	Player	Oh dear! Do any of them own a stall in the Al Kharid Bazaar?
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Well no, but one of them owns a moderately successful camel hire franchise.
2	line	Ali the Camel Man	Have you considered hiring a camel? Or perhaps purchasing one of your own? I can get you a discount.
2	line	Player	Never mind.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Rug Merchant
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Rug Merchant	Greetings, desert traveller. Do you require the services of Ali Morrisane's flying carpet fleet?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes please.
1	option	Tell me about Ali Morrisane.
2	line	Player	Tell me about Ali Morrisane.
2	line	Rug Merchant	What, you haven't heard of Ali M? Possibly the greatest salesman of the Kharidian empire if not all Gielinor?
2	line	Player	Hold on... yes I can place him now. He has me looking for his nephew Ali, I think he needs some help with his shop.
2	line	Rug Merchant	I wouldn't be surprised, he's mentioned to me on a few occasions that he is thinking of diversifying even further.
2	line	Player	You wouldn't have seen his nephew about then?
2	line	Rug Merchant	No it's been a quite a while since I last saw him.
2	action	other
1	option	Tell me about this magic carpet fleet.
1	option	I have some questions.
1	option	No thanks.
0	section	Talking to a Street urchin
1	line	Player	Hello there!
1	line	Street urchin	What do you want? Information?
1	line	Player	What would you know?
1	line	Street urchin	No one knows what's going on in the streets better than me. I live, sleep, eat and drink here. The fact that I'm so small means that people tend to ignore me which helps even more.
1	line	Street urchin	Do you need any other information?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Yes tell me about...
2	line	Player	Yes, tell me about...
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	The Menaphites
3	line	Player	Tell me about the Menaphites.
3	line	Street urchin	They're a bad bunch, always starting fights down in the Asp and Snake. Word on the street is that they're led by some deranged priest. Nobody's ever seen them though - they do all their deals through Ali 'the
3	line	Street urchin	Operator'. I reckon they're up to something, but they're such a close knit group that little ever slips out.
3	line	Street urchin	Do you need any other information?
3	action	initial
2	option	The bandits
3	line	Player	Tell me about the bandits.
3	line	Street urchin	There's not much to say, really. They're just a group of local thugs led by the biggest and strongest amongst them. If they have any other plans, I don't know about it.
3	line	Street urchin	Do you need any other information?
3	action	initial
2	option	The Mayor
3	line	Player	Tell me about the Mayor.
3	line	Street urchin	The mayor is a spineless coward! He never stands up to anybody. That's why the Menaphites are so strong now! He let them stay, and then they started causing trouble. When he realised his mistake, he hired a band
3	line	Street urchin	of local thugs to drive them out, but they saw how weak he was and turned on us too. Now we've got bandits and Menaphites, and the mayor isn't doing anything!
3	line	Street urchin	Do you need any other information?
3	action	initial
2	option	Ali Morrisane's nephew
3	line	Player	Tell me about Ali Morrisane's nephew.
3	line	Street urchin	I know him! He used to kick us when he caught any of us stealing from his stall.
3	line	Player	Do you know where he is now then?
3	line	Street urchin	He disappeared a little while ago. All I know is it had something to do with the gangs. Probably he scammed them. You'd have to gain their trust to find out more, m'afraid - if I get too close, they might disappear me
3	line	Street urchin	too!
3	line	Street urchin	Do you need any other information?
3	action	initial
2	option	The town
3	line	Player	Tell me about the town.
3	line	Street urchin	It's boring! We're not as big as Menaphos or as powerful as Al Kharid, and we've got a really nasty crime problem. It's no wonder so many grown-ups have left.
3	line	Street urchin	Do you need any other information?
3	action	initial
1	option	No thanks.
2	line	Player	No thanks.
2	line	Street urchin	Come back if you need any info about anything in the town.
2	line	Player	I will do thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Ali the Barman
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Ali the Barman	Good day. Can I help you with anything?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Yes, I'd like a drink please.
2	line	Player	Yes, I'd like a drink please.
2	action	
1	option	What's going on in town?
2	line	Player	What's going on in town?
2	line	Ali the Barman	Nothing much really. About what you'd expect from a sleepy little town like ours.
2	line	Player	What about those two gangs? That seems exciting.
2	line	Ali the Barman	They're paying customers, so I won't rock the boat if you don't mind.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Is there anything else I can help you with?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	No thanks, I'm ok.
3	line	Player	No thanks, I'm ok. Thanks for your time.
3	action	end
2	option	Yes, I'd like to talk about something else.
3	action	initial
1	option	I'm looking for Ali from Pollnivneach.
2	line	Player	I'm looking for Ali from Pollnivneach.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Well, I'm called Ali and I'm from here. Are you looking for me?
2	line	Player	Do you have an uncle called Ali?
2	line	Ali the Barman	Yes! All my uncles are called Ali!
2	line	Player	Oh dear. Well do any of your uncles have a stall in the Bazaar in Al Kharid?
2	line	Ali the Barman	Um... no.
2	line	Player	Well do you know if anyone here does?
2	line	Ali the Barman	That's a difficult question to answer. I don't know anyone else's uncles.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Is there anything else I can help you with?
2	action	above
1	option	The 'Asp and Snake'? What a strange name for a bar.
2	line	Player	The 'Asp and Snake'? What a strange name for a bar.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Maybe around these parts. Were you expecting it to have 'Ali' in the name?
2	line	Ali the Barman	I did think about calling it 'Ali's', but then it'd get confused with the Camel Shop, the Kebab House, the Mayor's residence...
2	line	Player	Yes, I get your point. It's a perfectly fine name.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Is there anything else I can help you with?
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Drunken Ali
0	section	Initial dialogue
1	line	Drunken Ali	Ahh, a kind stranger. Get this old man a drink so that he may wet his throat and tell you of the strange happenings in this town.
1	action	end
0	section	Using the first beer on him
1	line	Drunken Ali	Now where were we? Ah yes, Ali Morrisane's wayward nephew.
1	line	Player	What?! How did you know that's who I was looking for?
1	line	Drunken Ali	Er... well, he's a real scamp, that lad! I can't imagine a stranger would be asking after anyone else.
1	line	Player	Hmm. Well go on then, where is he?
1	line	Drunken Ali	I'd tell you more, but my throat is drying up. This desert climate is an inhospitable one. Get me another beer so that I can continue my tale.
1	action	end
0	section	After the first beer
1	line	Drunken Ali	Get this poor, thirsty old man another drink so that he may wet his lips and continue.
1	action	end
0	section	Using the second beer on him
1	line	Drunken Ali	You are too kind, now what were we talking about?
1	line	Player	Ali Morrisane's nephew.
1	line	Drunken Ali	Of course! I've known him since he was a wee lad. A right little mischievous beggar...
1	line	Player	Yes, I can imagine. Do you have any more recent information about him? Where is he?
1	line	Drunken Ali	Well now, if you had just asked me that in the first place I would have told you directly!
1	line	Player	You're right, I'm sorry for beating around the bush. Do you know where Ali's nephew is now, though?
1	line	Drunken Ali	I'd tell you more, but my throat is drying up. This desert climate is an inhospitable one. Get me another beer so that I can continue my tale.
1	action	end
0	section	After the second beer
1	line	Drunken Ali	Alas, my throat has dried up, and I cannot speak... perhaps another drink would help?
1	action	end
0	section	Using the third beer on him
1	line	Drunken Ali	Ahh, that hits the spot.
1	line	Drunken Ali	Now which of you two adventurers wanted to know where Ali's nephew is?
1	line	Player	I think you're seeing double.
1	line	Drunken Ali	Is this a double? No wonder I feel sick...
1	line	Player	Look, all I want to know is the whereabouts of Ali Morrisane's nephew.
1	line	Drunken Ali	Now is that his nephew from his side or his wife's? They have a huge family you see. I remember...
1	line	Player	No, no, no. Stop right there. You are not going to fool me into buying you another beer without first giving me some useful information.
1	line	Drunken Ali	But my lips are so dry, how can I possibly continue?
1	line	Player	Well if your lips are dry, I'll have to wring you like a wet cloth and squeeze out enough booze to fill another tankard. I'd reckon it would hurt though.
1	line	Drunken Ali	I see. Don't worry about me, I'll just have to soldier on. Now what do you want to know?
1	line	Player	For the last time, where is Ali Morrisane's nephew?
1	line	Drunken Ali	Oh, I don't know.
1	line	Player	Seriously?
1	line	Drunken Ali	Wait, wait! The last I heard he was in trouble with those gangs hanging around town. You won't get any answers out of them, though, not while they're feuding. Maybe if you were to solve that little problem...
1	line	Drunken Ali	Anyway, is there any chance of another beer?
1	line	Player	What do you think?
1	action	end
0	section	After the third beer
1	line	Drunken Ali	What were we talking about again? Yes yes, when I was a boy... no, that's not it.
1	action	end
0	section	Using an item other than a beer on him
1	line	Drunken Ali	Eh? What's this? I don't want that, get me a beer.
1	action	end
0	section	Asking the gangs
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Bandit	What do you want?
1	line	Player	I am trying to get to the bottom of this feud between you and the Menaphites.
1	line	Bandit	What's it to you?
1	line	Player	I'm just trying to understand why thieves of your repute would stoop to their level.
1	line	Bandit	Well, if memory serves me correctly, I think the hostilities began when they robbed one of our camels. A heinous crime.
1	line	Player	So if they offered a camel back as a gesture of goodwill, would you and the rest of the bandits cease your hostilities?
1	line	Bandit	Those Menaphites would never do that. They have no sense of honour.
1	line	Player	But if they did?
1	line	Bandit	I suppose so.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to a Menaphite Thug
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Menaphite Thug	What do you want?
1	line	Player	I am trying to figure out the feud that exists between you and the Bandits.
1	line	Menaphite Thug	Not much to figure out there, the problem is those thieving bandits.
1	line	Player	In what way?
1	line	Menaphite Thug	They are always stealing, starting fights and disrupting the lives of the townsfolk.
1	line	Player	Word has it that the Menaphites are also involved in unsavoury behaviour.
1	line	Menaphite Thug	Well, we also steal, start fights, and disrupt lives - but we do it with class! And the bandits definitely started it.
1	line	Player	How did 'they' start it?
1	line	Menaphite Thug	I can scarcely remember, it's been so long.
1	line	Player	Go on try.
1	line	Menaphite Thug	I think our leader once mentioned that they robbed one of our camels. A heinous crime around these parts.
1	line	Player	So if they offered a camel as a gesture of goodwill would you agree to cease hostilities?
1	line	Menaphite Thug	Those bandits would never agree to that. They couldn't afford even the mangiest excuse for a camel, never mind the desert traversing, four legged beauty that we would demand.
1	line	Player	But if they did?
1	line	Menaphite Thug	Well, I suppose so.
1	line	Player	Maybe if I got both gangs a camel, I could use the mutual good will to find out what happened to Ali's nephew.
1	action	end
