1	line	Player	Good news, the bandits have agreed to give you a camel in order to restore peace.
1	cond	If the player does not have a receipt:
2	line	Menaphite Thug	So where's the camel?
2	line	Player	Um... I'll get back to you on that.
2	action	end
1	cond	Otherwise:
2	box	You hand the doorman a sales receipt for the camel.
2	line	Menaphite Thug	A mere receipt? For a discount camel? I knew those bandits were cheap! Tell them that we have changed our minds and demand 10 camels in return for our
2	line	Menaphite Thug	mercy.
2	line	Player	Oh no... why do I bother?
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to a Bandit
1	line	Player	Good news, the Menaphites have agreed to give you a camel in order to restore peace.
1	cond	If the player does not have a receipt:
2	line	Bandit	So where's the camel?
2	line	Player	Um... I'll get back to you on that.
2	action	end
1	cond	Otherwise:
2	box	You hand the guard a sales receipt for the camel.
2	line	Bandit	What's this? A mere promise of a camel? From a discount camel store? I knew those Menaphites were cowards. Tell them that we have changed our minds and demand 10 full-price camels in return for our
2	line	Bandit	mercy.
2	line	Player	Oh no... why do I bother?
