0	section	Talking to a Street urchin
1	line	Player	Hey there!
1	line	Street urchin	Hi! Do you want to go rob some more people? I could do with some more money.
1	line	Player	I think I need to try a different tactic. Sorry, kid!
1	line	Street urchin	Well do you need any information then?
1	line	Player	No thanks, I think I have a fair idea of what is going on in the town now.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ali the Mayor
1	line	Ali the Mayor	I don't know what we did to deserve your presence here, but I for one am filled with regret.
1	line	Player	Well that's some show of gratitude! Can't I even get a 'thank you' for ridding your town of one of the gangs?
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Do you understand the concept of consequences?
1	line	Player	Er, I think so?
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Well, the consequences of your little piece of butchery are that the town is now even worse off. The bandits no longer have to waste time and energy fighting with the Menaphites and can direct all their attention
1	line	Ali the Mayor	towards making us miserable. So for your efforts I thank you, but I wish no-one had asked for your help.
1	line	Player	I'll set this town right before I leave, I promise.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Why do I wish that you hadn't said that? Your heavyhanded tactics scare me.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to a Bandit
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Bandit	Welcome! Your actions surprise me.
1	line	Player	What do you mean?
1	line	Bandit	It was brilliant the way you got rid of the Menaphite leader.
1	line	Player	Er... yes. Thank you.
1	line	Bandit	So will you run the rest of them out of town now?
1	line	Player	I don't know.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Cowardly Bandit
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Cowardly Bandit	Welcome. Our leader would be pleased to congratulate you on your disposal of the Menaphites who plagued this town.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ali the Operator
1	line	Ali the Operator	Why did you have to go and ruin everything? We had a beautiful future ahead of us, the town would have been ours!
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Maybe I wanted to make it MY town!
2	line	Player	Maybe I wanted to make it MY town!
2	line	Ali the Operator	I see. I knew the hunger for power would get to you eventually.
2	action	end
1	option	Evil megalomaniacs set on destruction should be opposed.
2	line	Player	Evil megalomaniacs set on destruction should be opposed.
2	line	Ali the Operator	Really? I thought you were meant to follow those types blindly, with unquestioning loyalty.
2	line	Player	Look, Gielinor is full of power mad evil-doers. I'm sure another will come along soon enough.
2	line	Ali the Operator	No... it just wouldn't be the same. I think I'll just wallow in self pity for a while.
2	action	end
1	option	I'm sorry, I didn't mean to upset you. Can we still be friends?
2	line	Player	I'm sorry, I didn't mean to upset you. Can we still be friends?
2	line	Ali the Operator	No, I think I'll just wallow in self pity for a while.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to a Villager
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Villager	You! You're the one that just made everything worse for us poor villagers!
1	line	Player	What?! I just single-handedly took apart one of the gangs that was ruining your town!
1	line	Villager	You adventurers! You never think, you just act. You think that by killing a powerful bad person, Gielinor will become a better place.
1	line	Villager	It's not that simple, things never are. You've created a vacuum, and now all that power will go to whoever's strong enough to take it.
1	line	Villager	Who do you think is stronger? Our elderly mayor, or the leader of the bandits?
1	line	Player	Oops. Sorry, I was just trying to help. So are things really that much worse?
1	line	Villager	Yes. Before your intervention the two gangs pretty much cancelled each other out. They spent most of their energy trying to kill each other.
1	line	Villager	Now that the balance is lost, the Bandits reign unopposed! They no longer have to deal with the Menaphites and heap misery upon misery on us. You must finish the job that you have started.
1	line	Player	You know, this adventuring lark is a lot more complicated than I thought!
1	line	Villager	If you're prepared to change something you must also be prepared to deal with the consequences! Now hurry up and fix this mess you created!
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What do you mean by fix the mess I created?
2	line	Player	What do you mean by fix the mess I created?
2	line	Villager	Do I have to spell it out to you?
2	line	Player	Would you please?
2	line	Villager	Just run the bandits out of town. Incidentally, I spotted their leader to the north-west just a few minutes ago.
2	action	end
1	option	Ok I'll get to it.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'll get to it.
2	action	end
0	section	Running the Bandits out of town
0	section	Talking to a Bandit
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Bandit	Welcome! Our leader wants to congratulate you on your swift disposal of the Menaphites who plagued this town.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Bandit Leader
1	line	Bandit Leader	Come here my friend, so I may embrace you. You have done us a great turn by disposing of those Menaphites.
1	line	Player	Don't jump to conclusions, I didn't do it for you.
1	line	Bandit Leader	Regardless, I am still very grateful. Now I have the town at my mercy.
1	line	Player	That's what I'm here to talk to you about.
1	line	Bandit Leader	Do you want a reward? A fee? I will not begrudge you that.
1	line	Player	No, I'm here to give you an ultimatum: either leave the town of your own free will or I will make you.
1	line	Bandit Leader	How the worm has turned. This no-name adventurer who was robbing, looting and poisoning not too long ago is now taking the moral high ground! Or are you trying to keep the whole town for yourself?
1	line	Bandit Leader	Pollnivneach is mine. You won't run me out without a fight. If you want us gone, you must defeat our strongest warrior in battle.
1	line	Player	Start packing your bags!
1	action	end
1	action	Bandit champion appears.
1	line	Bandit champion	Grrr
0	section	Talking to the Bandit Leader again
1	action	Bandit champion appears
1	line	Bandit Leader	Ali, come here!
1	line	Bandit champion	Grrr
0	section	Upon defeating the Bandit champion
1	line	Player	I have defeated your champion, now get out of town.
1	line	Bandit Leader	Adventurer... I have underestimated you. Perhaps we can come to an agreement. How about I work for you? Think of the riches you would make.
1	line	Player	Don't try my patience. Tell me where Ali is, and then get out of here?
1	line	Bandit Leader	Ali? Which Ali?
1	line	Player	Ali Morrisane's nephew! I know you gangs had something to do with his disappearance, so tell me where he is!
1	line	Bandit Leader	Ali Morrisane?! You fool. You've been had!
1	line	Player	What do you mean?
1	line	Bandit Leader	Go have a chat with these precious townspeople of yours. You'll soon learn the truth.
1	line	Player	I'll go talk to a villager now, just to prove you wrong. Now get out of here before I really get angry with you!
1	action	end
0	section	Finishing up
0	section	Talking to the Bandit Leader
1	line	Player	I told you to clear off! Why are you still here?
1	line	Bandit Leader	Adventurer... I have underestimated you. Perhaps we can come to an agreement. How about I work for you? Think of the riches you would make.
1	line	Player	Don't try my patience. Get out of here, and never return to this town again!
1	line	Bandit Leader	Ha! You fancy yourself the people's champion, do you? You are so naive. You don't even realise you've been tricked!
1	line	Player	What do you mean?
1	line	Bandit Leader	Go have a chat with these precious townspeople of yours. You'll soon see.
1	line	Player	I'll go talk to a villager now, just to prove you wrong. Now get out of here before I really get angry with you.
1	action	end
