1	action	The Bandit attacks the player.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Cowardly Bandit
1	line	Cowardly Bandit	You dog! You killed our champion and for that I hope you die a slow and painful death.
1	line	Player	What was that? Are you looking for a fight?
1	line	Cowardly Bandit	Me? No, no, I was just, er, complimenting your, that is - don't kill me, please!
1	line	Player	I wouldn't waste my time.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to a Villager
1	line	Player	Now are you satisfied?
1	line	Villager	Oh, it's you again!
1	line	Player	I have delivered you from two evil tyrants. Where's my thank you?
1	line	Villager	Thank you? For what? You come into our town. You rob, mug, burgle and kill and then expect respect and gratitude? Look, if it's praise and thanks you're looking for, talk to the mayor.
1	line	Player	I wonder why I bother sometimes! This place has been nothing but trouble and I still haven't found Ali's nephew.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ali the Mayor
1	line	Ali the Mayor	My thanks, adventurer. Your methods and motives may be questionable, but none can argue that you have delivered our little town from the wicked gangs who plagued it. I think things will change around here, now
1	line	Ali the Mayor	that our problems are at a manageable size.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	The least that I can do for you is answer your questions about the whereabouts of Ali Morrisane's nephew. He always was a mischievous young man, full of harebrained schemes.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	He dreamed of being the greatest salesman in all of Gielinor! Unfortunately, he was a little too good.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	He angered a number of people by coercing them into buying things they didn't really want. Completely within the law, of course, but the law could only protect young Ali for so long.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Once he angered the Menaphites and the bandits, I knew I could no longer protect him.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Under cover of darkness I smuggled him out of the town, and he's been gone ever since.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	I can assure you, however, that he is safe and well - and now that you have effectively ended the threat posed by the gangs, he can continue his business elsewhere. Last I heard he planned to open some kind
1	line	Ali the Mayor	of trade network with forty of his friends. A 'treasure trove', he claims. I'll believe it when I see it.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	I hope that helps you in your quest. If you speak to Ali Morrisane, do tell him that I wholeheartedly apologise for the way he - er, his family - has been treated.
1	line	Player	I think I may be able to help with one other thing. I heard that your house was burgled recently. If you're interested in recovering the goods, you ought to have a word with Ali the Operator.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Now, how would a passing adventurer know where to find my missing jewels?
1	line	Player	Er, let's just put it down to adventurer's intuition.
1	action	end
0	section	Reporting back to Ali Morrisane
0	section	Talking to Ali the Mayor
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Thank you once again. Have you spoken to Ali Morrisane yet?
1	line	Player	No not yet.
1	line	Ali the Mayor	Perhaps you should! I'm sure he's keen to hear word of his nephew.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ali the Barman
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Ali the Barman	Good day. Can I help you with anything?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Yes, I'd like a drink please.
2	action	
1	option	What's going on in town?
2	line	Player	What's going on in town?
2	line	Ali the Barman	Well since you gave the two gangs a good kicking, business has really taken off! Both gangs are spending all their gold here drowning their sorrows.
2	line	Player	That's great! So do I get a cut of the profits?
2	line	Ali the Barman	Get out of here, you cheeky rascal. A cut of my profits? As if!
2	action	end
1	option	The 'Asp and Snake'? What a strange name for a bar.
2	line	Player	The 'Asp and Snake'? What a strange name for a bar.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Maybe around these parts. Were you expecting it to have 'Ali' in the name?
2	line	Ali the Barman	I did think about calling it 'Ali's', but then it'd get confused with the Camel Shop, the Kebab House, the Mayor's residence...
2	line	Player	Yes, I get your point. It's a perfectly fine name.
2	action	previous
1	option	Could you tell Traitorous Ali that someone has poisoned his drink?
2	line	Player	Could you tell Traitorous Ali that someone has poisoned his drink?
2	line	Ali the Barman	What?! Poisoned drinks, in my bar?! My reputation would be destroyed if someone died here. Thank you adventurer.
2	line	Player	No problem at all.
2	line	Ali the Barman	Here, have a beer - it's on the house.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Thanks!
3	box	Ali the barman gives you a beer.
3	action	end
2	option	Thanks but no thanks, I don't drink.
3	line	Player	Thanks but no thanks, I don't drink.
3	line	Ali the Barman	Don't say that around here too loud please, it may catch and then I'd be out of business.
3	line	Player	You could always open up a non alcoholic fruit juice bar. You'd have less problems with drunken customers
3	line	Ali the Barman	You might be onto something there, but then what would I do with the drunken sailor?
3	line	Player	Who?
3	line	Ali the Barman	Drunken Ali. Oh never mind it's a long story.
3	action	end
2	option	Yuck! I don't like beer.
3	line	Player	Yuck! I don't like beer.
3	line	Ali the Barman	Fine, suit yourself. There's no need to insult me.
3	action	end
