0	section	Talking to Ali the Camel Man
1	line	Ali the Camel Man	Hello! Welcome back to my discount camel store. How are those camels getting along?
1	line	Player	Hey Ali!
1	line	Ali the Camel Man	Hello adventurer.
1	line	Player	Any news?
1	line	Ali the Camel Man	Not much really, I just want to thank you for what you have done for this town. I might even stick around now that business is better!
1	line	Player	Any grand plans?
1	line	Ali the Camel Man	Well I've been debating whether I should diversify into camel rental, too. Although I do have all these cages lying around... do you think there's a market for discount jackals?
1	line	Player	Maybe! Best of luck, in any case.
1	line	Ali the Camel Man	Thank you.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ali Morrisane
1	line	Ali Morrisane	Hello again my friend. I have heard nothing from my troublesome nephew. Have you any news of his whereabouts?
1	line	Player	Indeed I do. I was able to eventually learn of his fortunes, although it was a little bit more challenging than I originally thought.
1	line	Ali Morrisane	Well then please, tell me what has become of him. Nothing bad I hope.
1	line	Player	I was able to discover that he is quite the salesman. Perhaps too good. He has roughly forty people working under him.
1	line	Player	Unfortunately a number of people didn't approve of his sales techniques and as a result he is in hiding.
1	line	Ali Morrisane	You make an old man very happy. I'm so proud of young Baba.
1	line	Player	But he's considered a thief!
1	line	Ali Morrisane	Yes, by people with too much money and not enough sense. All willingly parted with their money and received what they purchased.
1	line	Ali Morrisane	Well, it seems I still am in need of an assistant...
1	line	Ali Morrisane	..but take the reward anyway.
1	box	Ali Morrisane gives you 500 coins.
1	line	Player	I've just been thinking Ali, there seems to be a few parallels between yourself and your nephew. Both of you are unscrupulous salesmen, both of you come from the same town and both of you no longer trade there.
1	line	Player	Were you sent into exile too?
1	line	Ali Morrisane	I have my reasons.
1	line	Player	No, now hang on, this seems to me like one of the strangest quests I have ever been involved with. I do not believe that a businessman like you would not know of a competitor, particularly a competitor as talented as
1	line	Player	your nephew.
1	line	Player	So what was your motive to get me to visit Pollnivneach? Was it concern for the towns people? Hmm. I don't think so, I'd say you would probably sell your grandmother if you could get a good price for
1	line	Player	her. What was the reason?
1	line	Ali Morrisane	My my, you surprise me, you're not as dumb as you look.
1	line	Player	Surely you didn't do all this to sell me a fake beard and headpiece.
1	line	Ali Morrisane	Ah, once again you underestimate me. I sold you far more than that.
1	line	Player	Really? Well I did buy some other odds and ends off you.... no hang on! I get it now, you're in league with Ali the Camel seller, the Kebab seller and the mayor aren't you.
1	line	Ali Morrisane	I like the word 'tourism'. Did you not enjoy your stay in Pollnivneach? Was there not action, intrigue and fun to be had, and did you not notice all the other tourists there too?
1	line	Player	I must apologise for ever doubting you. You really are the greatest salesman in all of Gielinor.
1	line	Ali Morrisane	Now that we both agree on that, may I show you my wares?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	No, I'm really too busy.
2	action	Quest complete!
1	option	Okay.
2	action	
